# Follow ADR 0001

All **new** code and docs in this repo MUST comply with [docs/adr/0001-modular-oop-and-delivery.md](docs/adr/0001-modular-oop-and-delivery.md). Do not silently weaken it.

## Python

- Put features under `scripts/<package>/`, not the repo root.
- One capability per module; one primary class per module.
- Public API: methods without `_` plus read-only `@property`. Internals: `_method` / `_attr` only used inside that class.
- Do not expose `YOLO`, `VideoCapture`, or other vendor objects as public attributes. Return project types.
- Return copies of mutable arrays from properties.
- `from_env()` (or similar) owns environment variables; do not sprinkle `os.getenv` across collaborators.
- Package `__init__.py` must not import OpenCV/Ultralytics at import time (lazy `__getattr__` for `run`).
- Prefer a `Protocol` over importing Ultralytics in domain modules (counting, geometry).

```python
# ❌
best_model.predict(frame)
print(detector._model)

# ✅
outcome = detector.infer(masked_frame)
snapshot = counter.tally(outcome.boxes)
```

## Docker / Compose

- `docker compose`, never `docker-compose`.
- One-shot services: `docker compose run --rm <service>` only. Never treat bare `docker compose up` as the app entry.
- GPU train: merge `compose.gpu.yaml`. Default `train` stays CPU.
- Inference CMD: `python -m scripts.traffic_analysis`.

## Docs

- README must match the tree (names, entry points, `sample_video.mp4` vs `data/sample_video.mp4`).
- Supersede ADR 0001 with a new ADR if you change these rules; do not “just this once”.
